+//! Which kind of completion the Node process of the TypeScript SDK resumes from before a read, which sets how deep
+//! the stack under that read already is.
+//!
+//! An `await` resumes on the microtask queue, and the queue runs on top of whatever native callback last settled a
+//! promise. libuv delivers an `fs.promises` completion from deeper in its loop than the exit of a child process, so a
+//! read that runs after a file system call has less room than one that runs after a registry or `plutil` run ended.
+//! Every read in the same chain of microtasks shares that depth, whichever function it sits in.
+
+/// The kind of completion a chain of microtasks resumed from.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
+pub(crate) enum ResumeBase {
+    /// An `fs.promises` call settled: a `stat`, `lstat`, `readdir` or `readFile` of the managed folders.
+    Fs,
+    /// A child process exited: the run of `reg.exe` that read the registry.
+    Tool,
+}
